<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anti-Fascist People's Freedom League</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as AFPFL</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anti-Fascist People's Freedom League was a Burmese nationalist coalition formed during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san">Aung San</a>. It turned against the Japanese in 1945, negotiated independence with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> after the war and governed the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> from 1948 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/u-nu">U Nu</a>, until it split in 1958.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anti-fascist-peoples-freedom-league.jpg" alt="Anti-Fascist People's Freedom League" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Havsjö · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_AFPFL.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
